# Intent: Timers and Alarms at finger size (owner review 2026-11-18, the physical standard in docs/design/screen-style.md; batch UX13f, audit docs/plan/screen-standards-audit.md). The timers page has rows 56 px high on an 8 px gap with a 56 by 56 Cancel at the right edge (it was 58 by 44, 2 px apart), at most two rows with a "+N more in Apps" line when more run, and three 96 by 56 quick starts in the 20 px text. In the Apps wall the Timers app's preset column and running rows are 8 px apart (they were 4) and the Alarms app has a 56 px Add button and 56 px rows on an 8 px gap, two showing and the rest scrolling. Display only: no safety, lock, cue, limiter or head-motion code.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_pages.cc, maipai_pages_core.h, maipai_apps_core.h (ours)
# Check after a flash: the timers page with one and two timers shows rows a finger can press with a Cancel at the right; a third timer shows "+1 more in Apps"; Apps then Timers has an even gap between the preset buttons and the running rows; Apps then Alarms has a tall Add button and rows with a gap.
# Kconfig: none

